      "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n## What does this PR do?\n\nFixes #7464. Label smoothing in vocabulary-parallel cross entropy now uses the global vocabulary size and global mean log-probability.\n\nThe current forward pass averages only the local vocabulary shard and can take `log(0)` after softmax underflow. The fix reduces the shifted-logit sum across the TP group before logits are exponentiated, then computes the global mean log-probability from that sum and the global log normalizer. Backward uses the same global vocabulary size.\n\nRelated: #737 and the closed, unmerged #5522. This implementation also addresses finite losses for large logits; it does not depend on #5522 being merged.\n\n## Validation\n\n- A two-process CPU/Gloo check of the current production autograd definitions passed against an independent float64 dense reference for smoothing 0 and 0.1, logits scaled by 1 and 1,000, and forward/backward. Maximum absolute loss residual: `2.83e-4`; gradient comparison passed at `atol=1e-7, rtol=2e-6`. That check uses eager helpers, not the CUDA JIT path.\n- Added a native TP=2 loss/gradient regression and extended the registered bit-exact replay test with large logits. These GPU tests have **not** been run locally.\n- `BASE_REF=main CHECK_ONLY=true SKIP_DOCS=false bash tools/autoformat.sh` completed successfully. Pylint reported the repository's existing unsupported `bad-builtins` option; the changed code scored 10/10.\n- `python tools/check_kernel_determinism_coverage.py --base-ref HEAD` passed for the uncommitted diff.\n\n## Pre-checks\n\n- [x] Added relevant unit tests.\n- [x] Updated the existing, registered determinism test.\n- [x] Ran the formatter and lint checks.\n- [ ] GPU functional and determinism execution.\n\nDraft pending native GPU validation and review. The commit is signed and includes a DCO sign-off.\n",
